A class defining __setattr__ intercepts every write, so a stored field value
cannot be trusted (here it stores a str into an int field). cbmc over-
approximates attribute reads on __setattr__ / __getattribute__ instances to a
nondet python_value, so c.x - 1 routes through the operator tag obligation and
the possible TypeError is reported. PLR-correct: VERIFICATION FAILED.
